WEBVTT

01:49.109 --> 01:56.116
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

02:00.120 --> 02:01.204
Any casualties?

02:01.287 --> 02:04.541
We lost three soldiers and four members
of the disease control platoon.

02:04.624 --> 02:06.626
One major was heavily injured.

02:06.709 --> 02:09.295
Most of the Joseon test subjects are dead.

02:49.627 --> 02:51.087
How beautiful was it?

02:52.213 --> 02:53.214
How did it move?

02:54.340 --> 02:56.217
Just how fast was it?

03:00.430 --> 03:01.431
Tell me.

03:01.931 --> 03:03.933
Tell me how perfect it was.

03:12.025 --> 03:16.863
6 HOURS EARLIER

04:44.284 --> 04:45.493
Excuse me, Major.

04:45.576 --> 04:48.121
I haven't seen the floating spores
in a while now.

05:42.759 --> 05:43.926
Help!

05:45.595 --> 05:46.971
Somebody help me!

05:52.810 --> 05:53.644
Lights!

05:53.728 --> 05:55.229
Quickly! Now!

05:55.313 --> 05:56.356
Aim!

06:09.786 --> 06:11.496
Do you see anything?

06:11.579 --> 06:13.373
No, sir. I can't make anything out!

06:31.974 --> 06:33.476
Help me.

06:36.979 --> 06:39.065
Please, somebody help.

06:44.362 --> 06:45.613
Help me!

06:46.155 --> 06:47.657
I don't want to die.

06:48.199 --> 06:50.910
Please… Please help me.

06:51.661 --> 06:52.662
Shut the door.

07:01.796 --> 07:04.590
Shut the door. Now!

07:28.531 --> 07:30.032
Don't stop!

07:30.700 --> 07:32.034
Shut it now.

07:34.036 --> 07:35.705
I said, shut the door.

07:36.664 --> 07:37.498
Hurry up!

07:56.309 --> 07:59.061
Help me, please!

08:07.028 --> 08:10.114
Please! Help me, sir!

08:11.908 --> 08:14.452
Shut the door. Do it now.

08:14.535 --> 08:17.205
I don't want to die. Please help me!

08:17.288 --> 08:19.540
Help me, Major Endo!

08:20.791 --> 08:23.836
- Let go.
- No!

08:23.920 --> 08:25.004
No, I won't!

08:25.087 --> 08:26.547
- The door won't close!
- No!

08:26.631 --> 08:28.174
It won't close because of you!

08:38.434 --> 08:39.936
Let go!

08:40.019 --> 08:42.188
Major Endo!

08:42.271 --> 08:43.189
Asshole!

09:45.751 --> 09:46.836
Answer me.

09:48.170 --> 09:49.589
Was our experiment

09:50.798 --> 09:51.882
a success?

09:54.093 --> 09:55.511
Please…

09:58.431 --> 09:59.724
destroy it.

10:02.351 --> 10:05.271
What you have created…

10:08.107 --> 10:09.191
is a calamity.

10:10.651 --> 10:13.654
Before it's too late,

10:14.780 --> 10:16.157
please destroy

10:17.158 --> 10:18.993
that creature.

10:30.504 --> 10:34.050
A calamity, you say?

11:20.262 --> 11:21.263
I see.

11:29.730 --> 11:33.067
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN OBSESSION AND PERSEVERANCE

11:33.150 --> 11:35.736
EPISODE 3
SIGNAL

11:49.709 --> 11:51.210
The tea is very fragrant.

11:53.295 --> 11:55.047
All thanks to you, Mr. Jang.

11:56.716 --> 11:59.677
My tea ceremonies have become
twice as enjoyable

11:59.760 --> 12:02.596
thanks to the elegant cups
you procured for me.

12:03.764 --> 12:06.851
Your pronunciation of the Joseon tongue
has become much more natural.

12:06.934 --> 12:11.230
Also thanks to you and the great teacher
you introduced me to.

12:23.075 --> 12:26.746
Oh, I heard that Ongseong Hospital
has shut down.

12:27.663 --> 12:29.081
Have you heard anything?

12:31.667 --> 12:32.668
Well,

12:34.211 --> 12:35.880
I did hear in passing

12:35.963 --> 12:39.550
that an unknown infection
has spread in there.

12:40.718 --> 12:44.430
The thing is, I've since lost contact
with a friend who was admitted there.

12:45.264 --> 12:49.518
If you know anyone inside,
I was hoping you could ask them

12:50.019 --> 12:53.022
about what it's like inside
and when it might open again.

12:54.106 --> 12:57.151
Is this because of the girl
named Myeong-ja?

13:00.988 --> 13:04.492
If so, it would be best
not to look for her.

13:14.460 --> 13:19.548
There is a Joseon saying that goes,
"A drowning man will grasp at straws."

13:21.133 --> 13:25.179
It means that a desperate man will cling
to anything, no matter how trivial.

13:28.015 --> 13:31.018
I'm that drowning man, Lady Maeda.

13:31.727 --> 13:35.898
You're more than capable of brushing off
my husband's threats, aren't you?

13:36.482 --> 13:39.902
If they were mere threats,
I would've done so.

13:41.445 --> 13:43.113
But I think he's serious this time.

13:44.865 --> 13:45.699
So?

13:45.783 --> 13:48.744
I intend to take this seriously too,

13:50.329 --> 13:51.997
so I can survive.

13:53.791 --> 13:56.752
You can't enter
Ongseong Hospital right now,

13:56.836 --> 14:00.631
but even if you do,
you won't find what you're looking for.

14:01.715 --> 14:05.469
So, you should look for another way,
Mr. Jang.

14:06.679 --> 14:09.265
I'm advising you as a friend.

14:19.483 --> 14:21.277
I need the blueprints for the hospital.

14:21.360 --> 14:23.487
You have pull
with the Governor-General's Office.

14:23.571 --> 14:25.739
Please bring me the most detailed prints.

14:25.823 --> 14:29.410
What's the point of getting the blueprints
if we have no way in?

14:29.952 --> 14:31.453
The hospital is shut down.

14:31.537 --> 14:35.207
All outsiders and even the suppliers
have been denied entry.

14:35.916 --> 14:37.459
There is no way of slipping in.

14:37.543 --> 14:40.004
Bring them to me before the day is over.

14:40.087 --> 14:41.672
They say it's an infection.

14:41.755 --> 14:45.342
God knows what disease it might be.
We might all kick the bucket.

14:45.426 --> 14:47.761
I'll go in alone, then. Okay?

14:47.845 --> 14:49.722
What if it's a lie?

14:49.805 --> 14:52.516
What if that sleuth girl lied
to save herself?

14:53.100 --> 14:54.810
It's possible, isn't it?

14:54.894 --> 14:58.314
The hospital's closed. There's no way out.
And the infection is spreading.

14:58.397 --> 15:02.526
She could be lying about finding Myeong-ja
to save her own skin!

15:07.156 --> 15:09.909
- Do you really think so?
- Think about it.

15:09.992 --> 15:13.829
How can she be in a hospital reserved
for high-ranking Japanese officials?

15:13.913 --> 15:15.664
There's no way she's there!

15:15.748 --> 15:18.584
I'll bet my entire fortune of 380 won.

15:18.667 --> 15:21.837
How can you be so consistently unlucky?

15:21.921 --> 15:22.796
What?

15:22.880 --> 15:26.425
Every card you draw is crap.
Every bet you make ends in a loss.

15:26.508 --> 15:29.762
Every time you gamble,
you get your pockets totally cleaned out.

15:29.845 --> 15:31.722
Hey, when has that ever happened to me?

15:31.805 --> 15:34.099
Myeong-ja is definitely in there.

15:34.183 --> 15:36.602
I just had it confirmed by Lady Maeda.

15:37.186 --> 15:38.812
Ishikawa's wife?

15:38.896 --> 15:42.107
Did that woman tell you
that Myeong-ja is in there?

15:43.734 --> 15:44.818
Did she?

15:44.902 --> 15:46.820
That broad said that? For real?

15:46.904 --> 15:50.240
I'll be getting inside Ongseong Hospital
by 10:00 p.m. tonight.

15:50.324 --> 15:51.992
Please prepare accordingly.

16:08.717 --> 16:11.261
WE FOUND MYEONG-JA

16:14.473 --> 16:18.435
Send a signal by 10:00 p.m.
to the east wing of Ongseong Hospital.

16:19.019 --> 16:22.356
Any recognizable signal will do,
such as smoke or a flame.

16:22.439 --> 16:24.608
You won't find what you're looking for.

16:24.692 --> 16:26.110
Please find a way

16:27.569 --> 16:28.737
to get them out.

16:28.821 --> 16:31.281
You should look for another way,
Mr. Jang.

17:02.354 --> 17:04.732
So, what has Jang Tae-sang been up to?

17:04.815 --> 17:08.360
Well, he's been busy all morning
moving about the town.

17:08.444 --> 17:09.319
But…

17:10.738 --> 17:11.780
But what?

17:12.448 --> 17:14.533
His route has been a bit strange.

17:18.662 --> 17:19.621
Mahjong?

17:20.831 --> 17:21.749
I win!

17:21.832 --> 17:22.833
Yes, sir.

17:22.916 --> 17:26.420
He played mahjong for an hour
at the general store of Wang the Chinese.

17:29.214 --> 17:30.883
FIREWORKS

17:39.516 --> 17:40.768
The next round is double.

17:42.561 --> 17:43.395
Will you accept?

17:44.188 --> 17:45.022
Sure!

17:47.107 --> 17:48.067
And then?

17:49.443 --> 17:53.739
He rode a rickshaw around the streets
of Bonjeong for 30 minutes.

17:54.865 --> 17:57.493
- He just rode around the streets?
- Yes, sir.

17:57.576 --> 17:59.745
Then lastly, he visited…

18:05.292 --> 18:06.126
A tailor shop?

18:06.210 --> 18:09.588
Yes, sir. He seemed to be getting
a new suit tailored.

18:09.671 --> 18:12.925
I'd like a suit in the bold style
that's popular these days.

18:14.384 --> 18:15.219
Yes, sir.

18:25.020 --> 18:29.108
This American-made pure wool
just came in from Tokyo last month.

18:30.109 --> 18:33.904
I think you'd prefer
the second option of fabric far more, sir.

18:40.494 --> 18:43.163
It was sent over from the Moonlight Bar
just last night.

18:55.717 --> 18:57.344
I'm here for afternoon cleaning.

18:59.847 --> 19:00.764
Go in.

19:01.348 --> 19:02.307
Yes, sir.

19:12.609 --> 19:14.027
CLEANING SUPPLIES

19:33.172 --> 19:34.756
Have you delivered the note?

19:34.840 --> 19:36.800
I passed it on to someone we can trust.

19:36.884 --> 19:39.344
By now, it should be
at the House of Golden Treasure.

19:40.304 --> 19:41.221
By the way,

19:41.722 --> 19:44.266
are you certain that Myeong-ja is in here?

19:44.349 --> 19:45.851
It seems so.

19:45.934 --> 19:47.269
Actually, last night…

19:49.771 --> 19:50.898
Don't shoot him.

19:52.316 --> 19:53.442
He's on our side.

19:53.525 --> 19:56.195
- What?
- But that's a Japanese soldier.

19:56.278 --> 19:57.654
No, I'm not!

19:57.738 --> 19:59.364
I'm from Joseon.

20:00.574 --> 20:02.993
I really am from Joseon.

20:20.469 --> 20:22.846
Now, let's take a look here.

20:28.644 --> 20:29.895
It's in good condition.

20:30.812 --> 20:32.314
But it's rather old.

20:32.397 --> 20:35.734
It was my family's source of income
for the past ten years.

20:36.902 --> 20:38.987
I sent my eldest
to medical school with it.

20:39.071 --> 20:41.448
The most I can give you is 90 won.

20:42.324 --> 20:43.575
Will you still pawn it?

20:44.159 --> 20:45.744
I don't need the money.

20:45.827 --> 20:46.745
Instead,

20:48.080 --> 20:50.290
could you please find my son?

20:51.291 --> 20:54.795
I heard he was evacuated from Bongrim
after getting wounded in the battle.

20:55.671 --> 20:57.256
But I've lost contact with him.

20:58.674 --> 21:01.510
I was drafted while attending
Gyeongseong Medical School.

21:02.886 --> 21:05.597
In Bongrim, China,
I got injured during battle

21:06.181 --> 21:08.517
and was sent here, Ongseong Hospital.

21:08.600 --> 21:11.812
After recovery, I was assigned
to the disease control platoon.

21:12.562 --> 21:13.397
Disease control?

21:13.480 --> 21:17.192
It seems that this hospital also has
a human experiment lab underground.

21:19.528 --> 21:21.905
I saw countless Joseon people
lose their lives…

21:24.199 --> 21:26.118
with my own eyes last night.

21:28.829 --> 21:30.247
What happened last night…

21:33.375 --> 21:34.543
was due to anthrax.

21:38.213 --> 21:40.340
I witnessed something like this
in Bongrim.

21:42.592 --> 21:45.470
An entire village
was stamped out by anthrax.

21:50.267 --> 21:52.894
It was so horrific
that I still remember it to this day.

21:56.106 --> 21:58.150
Those damn bastards!

22:03.530 --> 22:07.659
Did you happen to see a young man
in his early 20s among the dead?

22:08.160 --> 22:11.621
He is medium-height and has a black spot
next to his right ear.

22:14.750 --> 22:15.834
I'm sorry.

22:17.044 --> 22:18.754
I couldn't examine all the bodies.

22:21.715 --> 22:25.177
Many Joseon people are still being kept
in the underground prison.

22:26.219 --> 22:28.305
That's where I saw Myeong-ja as well.

22:38.023 --> 22:40.400
Don't move
until we finish sterilizing the area.

22:41.735 --> 22:44.446
It's dangerous,
so please stay where you are.

22:46.239 --> 22:48.283
You could die
just by touching the anthrax.

22:48.367 --> 22:51.495
So don't move and stay in that corner
until everything is sterilized.

22:52.079 --> 22:53.038
All right?

22:54.956 --> 22:56.708
You have to help me.

22:58.377 --> 23:01.880
Please find Commissioner Ishikawa
at the Police Bureau.

23:01.963 --> 23:03.548
Tell him I'm here.

23:03.632 --> 23:07.969
Myeong-ja of Spring Moon Hall…
No, tell him Akiko is imprisoned here.

23:08.762 --> 23:11.139
I'm sure he will reward you handsomely.

23:11.723 --> 23:12.724
Please.

23:13.934 --> 23:19.106
Please tell Ishikawa.
Tell him that I'm here, will you?

23:21.483 --> 23:22.651
Shut it!

23:22.734 --> 23:24.736
Keep quiet. Stay back!

23:37.541 --> 23:40.419
But there was nothing I could do for her.

23:41.169 --> 23:43.422
Because I was in the same boat as them.

23:59.771 --> 24:00.939
What are you doing?

24:07.237 --> 24:09.281
Get it together, Josenjing!

24:17.873 --> 24:20.000
Don't spill your filthy vomit!

24:29.968 --> 24:31.219
You Josenjing!

24:44.399 --> 24:46.276
Filthy Josenjing!

24:54.701 --> 24:56.870
There was only one way to escape

24:57.871 --> 24:59.122
this living hell.

25:07.589 --> 25:08.590
Mother.

25:11.968 --> 25:13.762
Please forgive me!

25:44.084 --> 25:45.126
Don't waste your life.

25:53.176 --> 25:55.303
The time will come when your death counts.

25:58.014 --> 25:59.224
You can die then.

26:36.928 --> 26:37.929
Who is she?

26:39.097 --> 26:40.181
Well,

26:41.516 --> 26:43.977
I don't know
who the woman in the drawing is.

26:45.228 --> 26:47.772
But I do know who drew this.

26:49.065 --> 26:50.275
He's Japanese.

26:52.319 --> 26:53.820
He calls himself a painter.

26:54.946 --> 26:55.864
His name was

26:57.032 --> 26:58.533
Sachimoto, I believe.

28:01.429 --> 28:03.306
What are all these?

28:03.890 --> 28:05.433
What have you drawn?

28:13.608 --> 28:14.526
Tell me more.

28:15.652 --> 28:17.570
Who does he work for? Where does he live?

28:18.363 --> 28:19.948
Do you like Chinese food?

28:20.865 --> 28:23.284
At 8:00 p.m. tonight. Sahaeru restaurant.

28:25.078 --> 28:28.081
I'm afraid I have no luxury
to enjoy Chinese food at the moment.

28:28.164 --> 28:30.500
I'm talking about Sachimoto, not you.

28:31.251 --> 28:34.587
We arranged to meet at Sahaeru tonight.

28:35.964 --> 28:37.882
- Tonight?
- At 8:00 p.m.

28:38.466 --> 28:39.467
Don't be late.

28:48.017 --> 28:50.770
You must be running
an interesting experiment.

28:51.521 --> 28:54.399
I heard you lost
an entire disease control platoon,

28:55.191 --> 28:58.278
along with stacks of Joseon test subjects.

29:00.071 --> 29:03.825
I only wish that your experiment
will have strategic value for us.

29:05.535 --> 29:06.870
What do you mean?

29:06.953 --> 29:10.582
Tokyo has been burned to ashes
from the recent air strikes.

29:11.291 --> 29:13.209
We are in dire need

29:13.293 --> 29:18.631
of a powerful weapon that could
turn the tides of the war in our favor.

29:20.508 --> 29:24.888
How about we make use
of that creature down below?

29:27.432 --> 29:29.392
It's too early to reach any conclusion.

29:31.186 --> 29:33.938
Its intelligence, its cognitive abilities,

29:34.022 --> 29:36.816
and whether it could be tamed or not

29:38.026 --> 29:39.944
haven't been confirmed yet.

29:40.528 --> 29:45.450
Every living thing in this world
can eventually be tamed,

29:46.159 --> 29:49.120
just as we have tamed Joseon.

30:34.040 --> 30:35.959
I've only gone down
to the second basement.

30:36.042 --> 30:38.461
This is the underground prison.
And Myeong-ja…

30:38.545 --> 30:39.379
PRISON

30:39.462 --> 30:40.713
…was here.

30:42.715 --> 30:43.550
How many guards?

30:43.633 --> 30:47.345
A pair of guards are stationed
every ten meters.

30:48.012 --> 30:49.013
They are all armed.

30:49.097 --> 30:51.933
Getting her out is going to be
as difficult as getting in.

30:52.016 --> 30:53.059
But…

30:55.019 --> 30:58.940
if you get her out,
is there a way to escape the hospital?

31:03.611 --> 31:07.115
Let's wait in our positions
until we get a signal from outside.

31:07.198 --> 31:09.325
You should head back to your platoon.

31:10.493 --> 31:13.329
No, I'll never return to that place again.

31:13.413 --> 31:16.875
If they search the ward looking for you,
it will cause us more trouble.

31:16.958 --> 31:19.377
They might even find out about these two.

31:20.211 --> 31:22.630
Then the entire operation would be over.

31:26.509 --> 31:28.303
We should all be able to escape.

31:31.055 --> 31:32.098
I'm sure of it.

31:34.642 --> 31:36.477
I'll see you later, then.

31:38.396 --> 31:39.314
Please…

31:41.566 --> 31:42.901
don't forget about me.

32:06.591 --> 32:08.176
Do you recognize it?

32:09.469 --> 32:11.512
- The layout of this floor.
- Yes.

32:12.513 --> 32:14.599
It's like the underground laboratory
back in Manchuria.

32:14.682 --> 32:15.516
LABORATORY

32:15.600 --> 32:17.435
It's worth trying, don't you think?

32:19.270 --> 32:22.106
You remember what happened in Manchuria.

32:24.150 --> 32:27.028
What went on
in that underground laboratory.

32:29.155 --> 32:31.407
What horrors the people went through.

32:31.491 --> 32:34.160
- Chae-ok.
- If the same thing is happening here…

32:36.955 --> 32:39.540
shouldn't we try
to do something this time?

32:43.044 --> 32:45.755
Let's wait at least
until the signal arrives.

33:12.240 --> 33:13.908
It's already been 30 minutes.

33:13.992 --> 33:15.827
Who are you waiting for anyway?

33:16.661 --> 33:17.578
A woman.

33:18.079 --> 33:19.414
A wooman?

33:19.497 --> 33:21.165
Not "wooman." A woman.

33:21.916 --> 33:22.750
There she is!

33:35.013 --> 33:36.931
Good work. Get yourself something to eat.

33:56.743 --> 33:57.994
Oh, excuse…

33:58.703 --> 34:00.413
Look who it is.

34:01.330 --> 34:03.041
Jang Ttai-sang of Golden Treasure.

34:08.796 --> 34:11.716
Could you let me through?
I have urgent business to attend to.

34:12.383 --> 34:14.302
Welcome. This way, please.

34:29.108 --> 34:32.445
I think we have
some unfinished business to settle first.

34:33.821 --> 34:35.823
Okay. I get it.

34:36.908 --> 34:40.661
If that's what you want,
come to my shop tomorrow morning.

34:41.412 --> 34:42.413
Sound good?

34:55.676 --> 34:57.095
- Sir…
- Yeah.

34:57.178 --> 35:00.014
You must be hungry.
Here, it's Joseon hotteok.

35:00.098 --> 35:01.099
Try it.

35:01.182 --> 35:02.183
Yes, sir.

35:05.561 --> 35:06.729
So good!

35:07.313 --> 35:11.067
These Josenjing folks
really know their way around food, huh?

35:13.402 --> 35:14.529
Sir…

35:14.612 --> 35:16.572
Do you think he'll be okay?

35:23.037 --> 35:24.038
Mori.

35:24.789 --> 35:27.959
Our job is to observe, not intervene.

35:28.835 --> 35:30.586
We observe, report,

35:31.629 --> 35:33.047
and receive orders.

35:33.131 --> 35:35.466
That's all there is to it.

35:37.260 --> 35:39.011
- Yes, sir.
- Go on, try a bite.

35:50.606 --> 35:52.525
Hang on. Wait.

35:52.608 --> 35:53.693
Just a second.

35:53.776 --> 35:55.361
We can resolve this with money.

35:56.320 --> 35:59.240
No need to bring swords
into this fight, right?

35:59.323 --> 36:02.660
Settle down, guys.
How much money do you want?

36:04.245 --> 36:05.163
Golden Treasure.

36:05.246 --> 36:06.539
Golden Treasure!

36:08.666 --> 36:09.500
What about it?

36:09.584 --> 36:13.337
Give us the House of Golden Treasure.
Then I'll spare your life.

36:19.510 --> 36:20.887
Let's not kid around.

36:21.387 --> 36:23.222
I told you, I'm quite busy right now.

36:23.306 --> 36:26.309
I'm supposed to meet someone at 8:00 p.m.
A very important person!

36:26.392 --> 36:29.395
Would you look at the time?
Look, it's almost time!

36:29.478 --> 36:30.313
I'll be off.

36:32.523 --> 36:36.694
Hey, you should think carefully
about who means more to you.

36:36.777 --> 36:40.698
Many apologies,
but you're just not my type.

36:41.199 --> 36:43.784
Please don't force me
to think so dearly of you!

36:44.493 --> 36:46.579
- Hey, Jang Ttai-sang.
- Tae-sang!

36:47.663 --> 36:49.498
It's Tae-sang, not Ttai-sang!

36:50.541 --> 36:51.792
Say my name again.

36:54.378 --> 36:56.214
Do you wish to die?

36:59.133 --> 37:00.218
Of course not.

37:01.260 --> 37:02.970
I might be a luckless guy,

37:03.763 --> 37:06.182
but I never wish to get killed
by a bunch of scum.

37:06.265 --> 37:07.600
Jackass!

38:46.866 --> 38:47.783
You there!

38:50.286 --> 38:51.537
What's going on?

38:52.413 --> 38:53.414
Look here.

38:54.415 --> 38:57.168
I'm Jang Tae-sang
of the House of Golden Treasure.

38:58.210 --> 39:03.090
These thugs are attacking me
for no apparent reason.

39:03.841 --> 39:05.092
Help me, Officer.

39:06.052 --> 39:09.263
We're just teaching
this stubborn Josenjing a lesson.

39:09.347 --> 39:12.641
You can just go on your way, sir.

39:12.725 --> 39:16.645
Look, they are all brandishing swords!

39:17.396 --> 39:19.231
My life is in danger!

39:21.650 --> 39:24.653
I don't want you causing a scene,
so go easy on him.

39:25.237 --> 39:26.155
Yes, sir.

39:26.238 --> 39:27.239
Officer.

39:27.907 --> 39:29.283
Officer!

39:30.868 --> 39:31.952
See that?

39:32.661 --> 39:35.081
This is the Joseon you're living in.

39:35.164 --> 39:38.709
And you're nothing but trash
with a lot of money.

39:39.794 --> 39:42.338
Filthy and pathetic

39:43.756 --> 39:47.343
Josenjing

39:48.344 --> 39:49.637
trash.

39:56.477 --> 39:57.436
Boss!

40:01.065 --> 40:01.982
You're right.

40:03.234 --> 40:05.194
This is the Joseon I'm living in.

40:07.488 --> 40:09.240
So give it a rest.

40:10.825 --> 40:12.535
I'm already pissed off as it is.

40:27.633 --> 40:28.801
Look!

40:29.677 --> 40:31.595
Josenjings never die!

40:35.349 --> 40:36.809
He's one tough nut.

41:07.631 --> 41:09.049
This won't do, Father.

41:09.133 --> 41:12.386
If we wait here any longer,
we will be wasting the whole night.

41:12.470 --> 41:14.763
I'll go out and look around the ward.

41:26.025 --> 41:27.943
If this place has the same layout,

41:28.027 --> 41:30.779
there should be a vent
that leads into the underground lab.

41:31.363 --> 41:33.824
- And the vent would be…
- Connected to the rooftop.

42:02.603 --> 42:03.604
Chae-ok.

42:03.687 --> 42:07.483
Should things get out of hand,
you must return without hesitation.

42:07.566 --> 42:08.400
Do you understand?

42:09.151 --> 42:10.486
I'll be back.

43:00.411 --> 43:02.538
Hurry! Get a move on!

43:20.055 --> 43:21.181
The blueprints?

43:22.099 --> 43:24.018
I got them as I was told to.

43:24.101 --> 43:26.270
But is this the right thing to do?

43:26.353 --> 43:29.023
We are basically pushing him
right into his grave.

43:29.106 --> 43:31.108
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

43:31.191 --> 43:32.943
Master Jang calls the shots.

43:38.574 --> 43:39.658
Is Tae-sang upstairs?

43:39.742 --> 43:42.036
No, he's out. What's the matter?

43:42.119 --> 43:45.289
An urgent matter has come up.
Where is he right now?

43:45.372 --> 43:46.624
I'm not sure.

43:51.045 --> 43:52.671
- Tae-sang!
- Sir!

43:52.755 --> 43:53.589
Master Jang!

44:11.231 --> 44:14.068
Please wait here for a moment.
I'll go after him.

44:14.151 --> 44:15.027
Sure.

44:59.530 --> 45:02.366
You're getting into sword fights now?

45:02.449 --> 45:04.076
For heaven's sake!

45:04.576 --> 45:08.330
What kind of rotten pricks
would be foolish enough to mess with you?

45:08.414 --> 45:10.999
Wait here.
I'm going to report this to the police.

45:11.083 --> 45:13.836
We'll go to the hospital first.
Get the car ready.

45:13.919 --> 45:15.504
Right, the hospital. Okay.

45:16.088 --> 45:19.049
Did you get the blueprints
for Ongseong Hospital?

45:19.133 --> 45:21.051
Of course I did!

45:21.135 --> 45:22.469
They are downstairs…

45:22.553 --> 45:24.096
Forget about the blueprints.

45:24.179 --> 45:26.306
Let's wrap the wound up
and go to the hospital.

45:26.390 --> 45:28.142
Yeah, the hospital first.

45:28.225 --> 45:31.478
I'm fine. Show me the blueprints, Mr. Gu.

45:33.105 --> 45:36.150
Disinfectants and antibiotics
aren't going to heal this wound.

45:39.945 --> 45:43.657
We don't have much time left
until 10:00 p.m.

45:43.741 --> 45:45.033
Sir.

45:45.117 --> 45:46.785
The blueprints now, Mr. Gu!

45:46.869 --> 45:48.078
Tae-sang, please!

45:53.250 --> 45:57.254
What could possibly be more important
than your own life?

45:58.630 --> 46:01.467
Is Myeong-ja worth
getting stabbed over like this?

46:02.718 --> 46:04.011
Is she really?

46:04.094 --> 46:06.138
- Mrs. Nawol.
- I don't want to hear it.

46:06.722 --> 46:09.933
Shut your mouth and go to the hospital.
Is that clear?

46:13.604 --> 46:14.521
Right.

46:15.189 --> 46:18.233
You're right, Mrs. Nawol.
Myeong-ja means nothing to me.

46:20.110 --> 46:21.028
But…

46:22.529 --> 46:26.116
those bastards are using her
as a ridiculous excuse to take my stuff.

46:27.659 --> 46:32.039
They're claiming what's mine as theirs
without a speck of shame!

46:32.790 --> 46:34.625
They even took our country.

46:35.501 --> 46:36.919
They can take anything.

46:37.878 --> 46:38.796
I suppose so.

46:40.672 --> 46:41.673
But…

46:43.926 --> 46:45.677
I'm going to hold out to the end.

46:47.971 --> 46:52.309
They can beat me up and knock me around,
but I'll fight like hell for what's mine!

46:54.770 --> 46:58.565
If I run away because they threaten me
and let them take what is mine,

47:00.234 --> 47:02.694
they will never get to learn
a proper lesson.

47:02.778 --> 47:03.737
Am I wrong?

47:04.321 --> 47:05.155
You…

47:06.907 --> 47:08.158
You were stabbed.

47:10.577 --> 47:13.163
You're seriously wounded, okay?

47:14.748 --> 47:16.625
This kind of wound doesn't hurt me.

47:18.460 --> 47:20.879
What hurts me is not a sword.

47:24.091 --> 47:25.509
It's my broken pride.

47:54.705 --> 47:56.206
You're Yeong-chun.

47:57.958 --> 47:59.877
I apologize for visiting at this hour,

47:59.960 --> 48:04.214
but there is someone
who wishes to see Master Jang.

48:40.751 --> 48:43.086
Wang. Open the door!

48:43.170 --> 48:44.671
It's Gu from Golden Treasure!

48:46.298 --> 48:47.299
Wang!

48:55.933 --> 49:01.355
LABORATORY

51:25.791 --> 51:26.875
Mr. Sachimoto.

51:28.001 --> 51:30.754
I've been out to buy some new supplies.

51:31.505 --> 51:33.840
There are a lot of items.
Could you let us pass?

51:37.010 --> 51:39.096
I'll send him out
as soon as I unload them.

51:39.721 --> 51:40.806
I can't allow that.

51:40.889 --> 51:43.225
No outsiders are allowed
to enter the hospital.

51:48.188 --> 51:52.609
Then go ahead
and report directly to Director Ichiro.

51:53.610 --> 51:54.444
Pardon?

51:54.528 --> 51:58.240
The director ordered me to bring these in,
so there's no choice.

51:59.991 --> 52:04.079
You better tell the director yourself
that you can't allow us in.

52:35.193 --> 52:37.237
Are you here to save us?

52:38.613 --> 52:39.531
What?

52:39.614 --> 52:42.868
I saw you coming down from the vent.

52:44.161 --> 52:46.371
Please save us.

52:46.454 --> 52:49.332
Help us get out of here, please!

53:38.006 --> 53:38.840
Hurry up!

55:06.052 --> 55:07.053
Damn it!

55:43.340 --> 55:44.257
Come on out.

55:46.718 --> 55:47.886
Oh gosh.

55:51.639 --> 55:53.099
I nearly suffocated in there.

56:00.523 --> 56:01.608
This way.

56:17.624 --> 56:18.541
CLOSED

58:00.351 --> 58:01.352
What's going on?

58:01.978 --> 58:03.938
Are you sure this is the meeting place?

58:04.481 --> 58:07.567
This is the only cleaning supplies room
on the first floor I know of.

58:10.528 --> 58:11.362
The signal…

58:14.657 --> 58:17.410
I think our timing was off
because the signal was delayed.

58:34.344 --> 58:36.888
The night breeze of Joseon
is so refreshing.

58:39.098 --> 58:40.183
Let's drink here.

58:40.850 --> 58:41.851
Yes, sir.

58:49.192 --> 58:51.569
I found whiskey in the storage room.

58:53.029 --> 58:54.656
So I snuck it out.

59:47.959 --> 59:49.544
Hey. Be quiet.

01:00:11.983 --> 01:00:13.276
Don't shoot.

01:00:20.074 --> 01:00:21.159
Don't shoot.

01:00:22.452 --> 01:00:23.536
Who are you?

01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:46.225
- Fireworks.
- What is that?

01:01:44.617 --> 01:01:45.702
Chae-ok!

01:02:45.678 --> 01:02:46.679
Forgive me.

01:02:48.931 --> 01:02:49.932
I'm late.

01:03:06.574 --> 01:03:08.534
What a sight.

01:03:28.513 --> 01:03:29.597
They succeeded.

01:03:30.932 --> 01:03:32.350
I'm not so sure.

01:03:34.685 --> 01:03:35.853
I hope they did.

01:03:43.528 --> 01:03:45.613
No, I'm not sure what's going on.

01:03:45.696 --> 01:03:48.324
Yes, of course.
Fireworks are banned in Gyeongseong.

01:03:49.075 --> 01:03:52.995
Yes, sir! I'll find the culprits
and report them to you immediately.

01:03:53.579 --> 01:03:54.539
Yes, sir!

01:03:57.250 --> 01:03:59.752
I'm heading over to the bureau. Get ready.

01:03:59.836 --> 01:04:00.670
Yes, sir.

01:04:16.185 --> 01:04:17.728
How beautiful.

01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:21.399
Have you found Myeong-ja?

01:04:22.108 --> 01:04:23.943
Where is she? Did you get her out?

01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:27.613
You can come out now.

01:04:53.931 --> 01:04:54.765
Careful.

01:04:56.934 --> 01:04:57.852
There we go.

01:05:07.820 --> 01:05:09.071
Wait.

01:05:10.489 --> 01:05:11.324
Where's Myeong-ja?

01:05:11.407 --> 01:05:13.576
Get these kids out of here first.

01:05:13.659 --> 01:05:16.245
What are you talking about?
Who are these kids?

01:05:16.329 --> 01:05:18.080
If you take the kids out of here,

01:05:18.706 --> 01:05:20.041
I'll go and find Myeong-ja.

01:05:38.559 --> 01:05:40.394
You have something to show me?

01:05:41.437 --> 01:05:42.271
Yes.

01:05:53.366 --> 01:05:54.200
Move.

01:05:54.784 --> 01:05:55.993
Get in there now!

01:06:24.480 --> 01:06:25.481
What is this place?

01:06:44.417 --> 01:06:47.211
I'm going to make that creature
recognize me.

01:06:48.838 --> 01:06:50.423
Every time I ring the bell,

01:06:50.506 --> 01:06:53.050
it will remember
and know that I'm feeding it.

01:06:53.759 --> 01:06:57.888
It will know who its master is
and whom it must obey.

01:06:58.639 --> 01:07:00.182
That's how I'll tame it.
